.TH GROTTO 1 "October 2026" "Grotto Preview 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grotto \- manage Nostr identities and review signing requests (Preview)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grotto
[\fB\-\-new-identity\fR | \fB\-\-preferences\fR] [\fIURI\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Grotto provides Home, Activity, Connect and Preferences for the session daemon.
Each consumer selects its own identity; management selection changes no other app.
Local NIP-55L apps need no pairing. Remote NIP-46 apps pair with explicit consent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new-identity
Open identity creation/import in the existing management window.
.TP
.B \-\-preferences
Open Preferences in the existing window (also available from the primary menu with Ctrl+,).
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Hidden compatibility alias for \-\-preferences in the unreleased 0.1.0 wave.
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication-service
D-Bus/login service activation without an unnecessary management window.
.SH URI HANDLERS
bunker:, nostrconnect: and local grotto: are supported activation schemes, not nostr:.
Supplied relays are previewed before identity choice and consent. A foreign
bunker link does not import an identity or delegate custody.
.SH BACKGROUND AND SECURITY
Closing a window destroys it, not the daemon. Ctrl+Q quits approval UI only;
already-authorized signing continues and a later request can summon review again.
Pause signing is the separate session-wide security action. Resume needs trusted
GUI confirmation; unlocking the desktop does not automatically resume.
.PP
Keys use native keyring custody. Client apps do not receive private keys; explicit
Grotto create/import/backup operations may handle them. Same-user malware is outside
the security boundary. Signing returns an event, not proof it was published.
.PP
Background review defaults on after disclosure; launch-on-login defaults off.
Native packages do not install an always-enabled autostart entry. Flatpak/AppImage
signer builds are experimental, not release-supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grotto-daemon (1)
.PP
